Hello @mitch\_Hsieh

There is a related [discussion](https://community.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus-embedded-software/disable-hardware-goodcrc-for-sop-messages-in-ucpd-for-active/td-p/891369) on this topic, and demo **USB Sniffer/ SPY mode** available on the **STM32G071B-DISCO** board.

When the Type-C port cover (the blue door) is open, the board enters this mode, enabling it to monitor USBPD communication between a USB PD charger and a PC. In SPY mode, the board does not actively participate in the communication but instead captures trace data for analysis. This is particularly useful for debugging

1. Configure hardware for sniffing [Initialize\_USBPD\_Spy](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeG0/blob/abbbbed4adffb8715a922ea0b81ae9e3141b3cb3/Projects/STM32G071B-DISCO/Demonstrations/USBPD_Analyzer/Src/demo_disco.c#L407)();

```

husbpd = USBPD_HW_GetUSPDInstance(0);

LL_UCPD_StructInit(&settings);

LL_UCPD_Init(husbpd, &settings);

LL_UCPD_SetRxOrderSet(husbpd, LL_UCPD_ORDERSET_SOP | LL_UCPD_ORDERSET_HARDRST);

LL_UCPD_Enable(husbpd);

LL_UCPD_SetccEnable(husbpd, LL_UCPD_CCENABLE_CC1CC2);

```

2. Prepare UCPD RX + DMA [Intialize\_RX\_processing](https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/STM32CubeG0/blob/abbbbed4adffb8715a922ea0b81ae9e3141b3cb3/Projects/STM32G071B-DISCO/Demonstrations/USBPD_Analyzer/Src/demo_disco.c#L2068)(CC1) since it is attached

3. Launch DEMO\_Task\_SPY

I hope this could be helpful
